      "value": "@{603b04282fa90e5c53608eb6|full_name} Again, this is why I'm not certain if this is a bug or feature, because yes, this only started happening with the latest update and there's no mention of this being a change in the release notes. Now, there's already a system in place to check which hand last pressed the trigger in order to determine which hand will generate a pointing beam with interactive objects in an actual world so it's possible this feature simply got accidentally grouped with the holoporting cursor and now both are behaving this way. :P",
